{
  "id": "COMPOUND:16764 - PROTEIN:5856",
  "verbalization": "Iriskumaonin methyl ether is implicated in the biological activity against SNU-387 through a series of mechanistic pathways. The compound directly targets MOVP-3, which is a target of the compound (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol, which in turn targets SNU-387. This suggests a direct interaction between Iriskumaonin methyl ether and SNU-387 via a complex cascade of molecular targets. Additionally, Iriskumaonin methyl ether is also shown to target Hepatocyte and Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which are both targets of Neridienone A, which also targets SNU-387. These findings collectively support a potential mechanism by which Iriskumaonin methyl ether may exert its effects on SNU-387, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence suggests a multi-tiered pathway involving multiple targets, but the core mechanism remains unclear without further experimental validation.",
